  "gaps": [
    "The capture spans parts of three programs (end of History, full BS in Homeland Security, start of BA in Humanities); this ledger assumes the BS in Homeland Security, the only program fully captured. Confirm the intended program.",
    "The program table prints only a combined 84-credit 'Remaining General Education and Elective Courses' block; the separate elective credit amount for this major is not printed. The 41-credit general education framework (Communications 12, Mathematics 3, Arts and Humanities 6, Behavioral and Social Sciences 6, Biological and Physical Sciences 7, Research and Computing Literacy 7) applies within it, and CIFS 300 may count toward general education, so the exact gen-ed/elective split is not stated for this program.",
    "Residency is stated only at the degree level, not per course: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) at UMGC, half the major credits at UMGC, and at least 15 upper-level credits (300–499) at UMGC. No individual course is marked as institution-only.",
    "Grade rules: a minimum grade of C is required for courses applied to the major and a 2.0 overall GPA. WRTG 112 must be completed with C- or better within the first 24 credits. Mathematics must be completed within the first 24 credits. The professional exploration course must be taken within the first 6 credits.",
    "At least half the major credits must be earned through graded coursework. The capture does not state how this interacts with specific transfer or credit-by-exam sources for this major.",
    "Course-level prerequisites for the HMLS/EMGT/PSAD courses are not included in the capture."
  ],
